## 4️⃣ Error Handling Strategy & Fault Tolerance  

### 4️⃣1 Error Hierarchy (Domain → Application → Infrastructure)

```ts
// src/application/common/DomainError.ts
export abstract class DomainError extends Error {
  public readonly isDomain = true;
}

// Validation errors (business rule violations)
export class ValidationError extends DomainError {
  constructor(message: string) { super(message); this.name = 'ValidationError'; }
}

// Repository‑level errors (e.g. constraint violation)
export class PersistenceError extends DomainError {
  constructor(message: string, public readonly cause?: unknown) {
    super(message); this.name = 'PersistenceError';
  }
}

// Unexpected runtime errors (wrapped for safety)
export class UnexpectedError extends DomainError {
  constructor(message: string, public readonly cause?: unknown) {
    super(message); this.name = 'UnexpectedError';
  }
}
```

### 4️⃣2 Result/Either Wrapper (to avoid throwing in async flow)

```ts
// src/application/common/Result.ts
export type Result<T, E extends DomainError = DomainError> =
  | { ok: true;  value: T }
  | { ok: false; error: E };

export const Ok = <T>(v: T): Result<T> => ({ ok: true, value: v });
export const Err = <E extends DomainError>(e: E): Result<never, E> => ({
  ok: false,
  error: e,
});
```

### 4️⃣3 Global Express Error Middleware (Framework Layer)

```ts
// src/interfaces/middleware/errorHandler.ts
import { Request, Response, NextFunction } from 'express';
import { DomainError } from '../../application/common/DomainError';

export function errorHandler(
  err: unknown,
  _req: Request,
  res: Response,
  _next: NextFunction,
) {
  if (err instanceof DomainError) {
    const status = err instanceof ValidationError ? 400 : 500;
    res.status(status).json({ error: err.name, message: err.message });
    return;
  }
  // fallback – unknown error
  console.error('Unexpected error:', err);
  res.status(500).json({ error: 'UnexpectedError', message: 'Internal server error' });
}
```

### 4️⃣4 Fault Tolerance (Infrastructure)

| Concern                     | Technique                                               | Where Applied |
|-----------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------|---------------|
| **Transient DB failures**   | `typeorm`/`prisma` built‑in retry (max 3 attempts)       | `OrderRepository` |
| **Circuit‑breaker**          | `opossum` wrapper around repository calls                | `OrderRepository` |
| **Idempotent writes**       | `INSERT … ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING` (PostgreSQL)          | `add` method |
| **Timeouts**                | `Promise.race([operation, timeoutPromise])` (5 s)       | Service layer |
| **Logging & Correlation**   | `winston` + request‑id (express‑request‑id)              | All outer layers |

